# Quartr MCP is the default (no API access)

Bobby does not have Quartr REST API access. There is no `QUARTR_API_KEY`.
Never ask for one. Never treat `--use-quartr-rest`, `quartr_history_import`,
or `QuartrApiClient` as the pull path.

## Always do this

1. Pull transcripts with **Cursor Quartr MCP**: `search_companies` →
   `list_events` → `read_transcript` (and `section: "qna"` for the tail
   when `nextFromTimestamp` is set).
2. Write earnings calls to
   `Structured Narrative/transcripts_raw/{TICKER}_{PERIOD}.txt`
   via `scripts/_write_quartr_mcp_transcript.py` (merge full + Q&A windows
   by `paragraphId` if paginated).
3. Onboard with `--skip-pull` so Roz consumes the MCP-seeded files.
   Conferences go to `data/conf_transcripts/{TICKER}/{eventId}.json` and
   `scripts/_desk_conf_ingest.py --transcript-file`.

## Never do this

- Propose setting a Quartr API key
- Fail an onboard because REST is unset and stop
- Use ROIC as the default (`--allow-roic-fallback` is opt-in only)
